            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>The groups are the Ministry's own: they follow how industries are organised (engineering, chemicals, textiles) rather than the customs chapters. Each bar is the latest full year; the circle is the same group fifteen years earlier, in dollars of each year, so some of the growth is inflation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of {T.groups.lastFy}</span>
            <p>The largest export groups were <span id="ex-s-1">–</span>, <span id="ex-s-2">–</span> and <span id="ex-s-3">–</span>. Electronics rose from <b id="ex-s-el0">–</b> to <b id="ex-s-el1">–</b>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:88px">
      <figure id="cb-buy" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3><span id="h-buy">–</span></h3>
            <div class="sub">Imports by the same 21 groups, US$ billion, {T.groups.firstFy} (circle) and {T.groups.lastFy} (bar).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-buy">–</div><div class="c">petroleum imports, {T.groups.lastFy}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
