  <!-- § 07 partners: inputs trade-partners-balance-fy, trade-partners-*-fy, trade-partners-long, trade-regions-*-fy -->
  <section>
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="no">07</span><h2>With whom</h2><span class="line"></span><span class="unit">US$ billion, financial years</span></div>
    <div class="break">
      <figure id="cb-partners" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3><span id="h-partners">–</span></h3>
            <div class="sub">Trade balance with India's ten largest deficit partners and ten largest surplus partners, US$ billion, {T.partners.fy}. Exports minus imports.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-partners">–</div><div class="c">deficit with China, {T.partners.fy}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone"><div id="plot-partners" style="position:relative"></div></div>
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: Ministry of Commerce, TradeStat (DGCI&amp;S), MEIDB region-wise tables, March cumulatives. Balance computed as exports minus imports.</span>
            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href="https://tradestat.commerce.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>A deficit with one country is not a problem in itself: India buys crude from the Gulf and Russia because it produces far too little of its own (see the crude oil plate below), and pays for it partly with what it sells to the United States and Europe. Countries are where goods come from or go to as declared at customs, so goods routed through the UAE or Singapore count against those hubs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of {T.partners.fy}</span>
            <p>India ran a deficit with <b id="ex-p-n">–</b> of <span id="ex-p-of">–</span> partners. Deficit with China <b id="ex-p-cn">–</b>; surplus with the United States <b id="ex-p-us">–</b>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:88px">
      <figure id="cb-chinaus" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3><span id="h-chinaus">–</span></h3>
            <div class="sub">Trade balance with China and with the United States, US$ billion, financial years 2009-10 to {fyOf(T.chinaus.dates.at(-1))}.</div>
          </div>
