            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href="https://tradestat.commerce.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>This is a separate ministry table from the monthly partner tables above, so it reaches back to 2009-10. The two agree where they overlap but are drawn apart.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of {fyOf(T.chinaus.dates.at(-1))}</span>
            <p>India bought <b id="ex-cu-cnm">–</b> from China and sold it <b id="ex-cu-cnx">–</b>. It sold the United States <b id="ex-cu-usx">–</b> and bought <b id="ex-cu-usm">–</b>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:88px">
      <figure id="cb-cxc" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>What goes to America, and what comes from China</h3>
            <div class="sub">The ten largest HS chapters in India's exports to the United States and its imports from China, US$ billion, <span id="sub-cxc">–</span>.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-cxc">–</div><div class="c">electrical machinery from China</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone"><div id="plot-cxc" style="position:relative"></div></div>
