            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Read the two lists against each other. Where a chapter appears on both, India is often buying parts, machines and chemicals from China to make goods it then sells abroad: electrical machinery bought as components can leave as finished phones. A chapter is a broad shelf, so the same number can hide very different goods; the every-cut table at the end goes down to the heading.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of {T.cxc ? T.cxc.us.fy : T.partners.fy}</span>
            <p>Top export to the United States: <span id="ex-x-us1">–</span>, <b id="ex-x-us1v">–</b>. Top import from China: <span id="ex-x-cn1">–</span>, <b id="ex-x-cn1v">–</b>.</p>
          </div>
