  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Commodity and partner detail: Ministry of Commerce and Industry, TradeStat (tradestat.commerce.gov.in), which publishes DGCI&amp;S customs data: the monthly export-import data bank (MEIDB), principal-commodity tables (FTPA and FTSPCC). The long history and the oil split: RBI, Database on Indian Economy, through the owner's local mirror of DBIE. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked against the Ministry's quick-estimates release of 13 August 2026: gold imports for July 2025 (US$ 3,974 million), rice exports (US$ 921 million) and coal imports (US$ 2,361 million) match these tables to the million, and 2025-26 exports total US$ 441,452 million in both.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Every TradeStat table this guide uses is archived as served. A month's value is the revised print from the table a year later where one exists, else its own final print; the principal-commodity monthly values are differences of the published running totals. Balances, growth rates and shares are computed here. Nothing is estimated or filled in.</p>
        <p>TradeStat's annual bank (EIDB) is not used: its 2023-24 commodity tables count every shipment twice (the chapters add up to exactly twice the printed total), which is why some figures for that year circulate at double their true size.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Three prints per month (provisional, final, revised final), recorded per value. The 6- and 8-digit codes changed with HS 2022 in April 2023 and are kept in separate yearly files; 2- and 4-digit series run through. The RBI's index numbers sit on three bases (1978-79, 1999-2000, 2012-13), never joined; its export volume index for 2025-26 is withheld as a broken print.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from data to {PT.long}. Revised each month when the Ministry publishes the next tables.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>India Atlas, merchandise trade</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2">–</span></span>
      <span>Set in Source Serif 4 and Golos Text</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

